lse,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"lX0+d","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"Done"}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"9e228984-e9b4-418d-8677-04dc8d35c391","type":"message","user":"U04R546B8JD","text":"great, thanks mate!","ts":"1742576029.661619","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ddzlv","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"great, thanks mate!"}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"7636e0f5-6e8c-4dcd-999f-4d17ae9590dc","type":"message","user":"U04R546B8JD","text":"hey Hrusi! we’re having an issue getting emails through to our contacts at JP Morgan Chase. Lizzie sent a couple of few weeks ago that didn’t make it to their inboxes, and I’ve tried sending an email both from my The News Movement alias and Caliber alias to no avail.\n\ndo you have any suggestions? is there anything we can do on our end, or anything they can do on theirs?","ts":"1760957259.109669","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"pvWIz","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"hey Hrusi! we’re having an issue getting emails through to our contacts at JP Morgan Chase. Lizzie sent a couple of few weeks ago that didn’t make it to their inboxes, and I’ve tried sending an email both from my The News Movement alias and Caliber alias to no avail.\n\ndo you have any suggestions? is there anything we can do on our end, or anything they can do on theirs?"}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"852e3e90-198a-45fa-88e2-788666f3444b","type":"message","user":"U05BV05GYQH","text":"Hi Will - could you share a bit more context on the issue? Are the emails going to their spam folder, or could there be a rule on their end that’s automatically deleting, forwarding, or archiving them? They might say no, but sometimes they have broader filters which could be unintentionally filtering more.\n\nIf they are receiving them but they land in spam, getting the original message headers would help us check a few things on our side.\n\nThe fact that TNM emails aren’t being delivered either suggests it’s likely an overly aggressive filter on their end - either personal settings or at the mail server level.","ts":"1760985749.465689","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"2u3+v","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"Hi Will - could you share a bit more context on the issue? Are the emails going to their spam folder, or could there be a rule on their end that’s automatically deleting, forwarding, or archiving them? They might say no, but sometimes they have broader filters which could be unintentionally filtering more.\n\nIf they are receiving them but they land in spam, getting the original message headers would help us check a few things on our side.\n\nThe fact that TNM emails aren’t being delivered either suggests it’s likely an overly aggressive filter on their end - either personal settings or at the mail server level."}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"D35262A9-ACBB-477B-8D07-AACAF14FC394","type":"message","user":"U04R546B8JD","text":"they aren’t even able to find them in spam…","ts":"1760987348.383799","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"JruCj","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"they "},{"type":"text","text":"aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" even able to find them in spam"},{"type":"text","text":"…"}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"3AD74614-3867-4A31-9591-7DBD7EF00B74","type":"message","user":"U04R546B8JD","text":"so, is the only thing we can suggest that they escalate the issue with tech support/IT on their end? ","ts":"1760987392.964079","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"2tg08","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"so, is the only thing we can suggest that they escalate the issue with tech support/IT on their end? "}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"e3b91c97-2b58-44bd-ba31-898ae6df17f6","type":"message","user":"U05BV05GYQH","text":"Do they have a quarantine queue? Some mail servers will hold the email there until the user goes and says they're ok. If not, they'd need to escalate to their IT.","ts":"1760987433.653539","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"vnWuw","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"Do they have a quarantine queue? Some mail servers will hold the email there until the user goes and says they're ok. If not, they'd need to escalate to their IT."}]}]}]},{"client_msg_id":"0C9861FC-79A8-47F6-92BF-CB25F57B71D1","type":"message","user":"U04R546B8JD","text":"shall ask! ","ts":"1760988270.211749","team":"T01E0D9F1NW","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"metadata":{"event_type":"","event_payload":null},"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ur1rH","elements":[{"type":"rich_text_section","elements":[{"type":"text","text":"shall ask! "}]}]}]}]}
